He pretended there was a clear opening for him and then took it away last second.

10
00:02:12,780 --> 00:02:15,100
Bet that four-eyed douche thinks he's smart.

11
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:17,960
Well, he did lose his set because of him.

12
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:22,320
Come to think of it, should I be scared that Coach hasn't raged at us for it yet?

13
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:23,380
Shirabu.

14
00:02:29,220 --> 00:02:29,660
Yes?

15
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:36,060
Judging by the look on your face, I can tell you already know.

16
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:43,020
You all right there, Shirabu?

17
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:47,400
You know, if this had been a practice match, you would have slapped me.

18
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:49,000
You think so?

19
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:51,620
It's not like your set was the only screw-up of the game.

20
00:02:51,740 --> 00:02:53,360
This stuff happens to the best of us.

21
00:02:54,180 --> 00:02:56,080
This wasn't just a simple mistake.

22
00:02:56,760 --> 00:02:58,120
Shirabu!

23
00:03:01,860 --> 00:03:02,140
Oh.

24
00:03:02,480 --> 00:03:02,780
Oh.

25
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:18,020
Let's start it off right.

26
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:21,240
Cover it.

27
00:03:21,240 --> 00:03:26,980
Shake it off! Set's just starting.

28
00:03:27,460 --> 00:03:27,760
Yeah!

29
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:36,820
Sure, Torizawa.

30
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:39,380
Was not shaken up from that last set.

31
00:03:39,940 --> 00:03:40,320
Yeah.

32
00:03:41,220 --> 00:03:41,700
Yeah!

33
00:03:42,320 --> 00:03:45,740
I can tell that their setter isn't letting the last round get him down.

34
00:03:46,180 --> 00:03:48,560
If anything, he's more focused now.

35
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:52,680
I have to hand it to them.

36
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:54,460
That attack was praiseworthy.

37
00:03:55,220 --> 00:03:58,380
I always get a bit awestruck when someone performs at the top of their game.

38
00:04:00,140 --> 00:04:00,820
But...

39
00:04:04,740 --> 00:04:05,860
All right!

40
00:04:06,100 --> 00:04:08,720
Sure, your tosses have been stellar all game.

41
00:04:08,920 --> 00:04:09,300
Thanks.

42
00:04:10,640 --> 00:04:12,500
Back then, our team was pretty strong.

43
00:04:13,320 --> 00:04:17,600
But in the end, it would often come down to these two schools duking it out for the championship.

44
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:24,400
Kitagawa first made up for the lack of size with their strategies using their incredible speed and skill combinations.

45
00:04:24,940 --> 00:04:27,600
That refinement is something we could have tried to mimic.

46
00:04:27,900 --> 00:04:32,200
And from my perspective as a setter, Mikawa came across as a monster out there.

47
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:37,840
However, I found myself pushing aside things like skilled teamwork and group attacks.

48
00:04:38,540 --> 00:04:41,760
I became captivated with height and power.

49
00:04:44,860 --> 00:04:49,080
These attributes were the embodiment of the perfect playstyle for me.

50
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:55,040
The kind of style where even if you play poorly, you can pull off a clutch win with just one open toss.

51
00:04:55,580 --> 00:04:59,140
The kind of style where this setter doesn't need to control the whole game.

52
00:04:59,140 --> 00:05:01,820
I'm gonna go to Shira Torizawa.

53
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:04,140
Hmm? What?

54
00:05:04,520 --> 00:05:06,340
I'm going to play with the strongest players.

55
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:08,720
So I can play at that level.

56
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:16,060
This was the epitome of volleyball to me.

57
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:31,200
I'll become the setter that stands up the least.

58
00:05:36,200 --> 00:05:37,140
Damn it!

59
00:05:38,420 --> 00:05:39,980
Focus! We'll get next!

60
00:05:40,180 --> 00:05:41,560
Hey, are you okay, Nishinoya?

61
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:49,760
There's no getting around that height is a huge advantage in life.

62
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:54,600
And right now, Ushiwaka has that huge advantage over all of us on the team.

63
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:57,300
But a Libro doesn't give a crap about that.

64
00:05:57,720 --> 00:06:01,280
The only one who's equal to him would be me.

65
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:23,700
I assume since you move so quickly, that you'd be good at blocks and receives, too.

66
00:06:23,700 --> 00:06:31,220
Since I outclass you in pure height, you think your clumsy technique will make up for it?

67
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:38,060
Clumsy, inept, unrefined, oafish, blunderous.

68
00:06:38,280 --> 00:06:38,660
Got it?

69
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:39,800
Got it!

70
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:45,540
Hey! Quit screwing around!

71
00:06:45,540 --> 00:06:50,620
You know, you and Ushiwaka have more in common than you realize.

72
00:06:51,440 --> 00:06:51,840
Huh?

73
00:06:52,620 --> 00:06:54,120
You really think so?

74
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:57,700
Well, I don't see myself quite at his level, but I could see how you'd compare us.

75
00:06:58,360 --> 00:07:00,360
That's not how I meant it, you big dummy!

76
00:07:01,820 --> 00:07:03,060
Shira Torizawa!

77
00:07:05,160 --> 00:07:06,440
Shira Torizawa!

78
00:07:06,460 --> 00:07:07,440
Come take a breather!

79
00:07:08,260 --> 00:07:10,400
So now you've seen it up close and personal.

80
00:07:10,760 --> 00:07:13,880
You've seen firsthand what it's like to take on a team like Shira Torizawa.

81
00:07:14,500 --> 00:07:17,280
And what you are doing is working, so stick with it.

82
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:23,500
However, we're still at a major disadvantage, so don't let yourselves get too cocky.

83
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:28,760
I need to emphasize that we need to keep the blocking together and stay out of the receiver's way.

84
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:33,400
And don't you ever forget, our true power is teamwork, playing together.

85
00:07:33,980 --> 00:07:35,080
That's how we win!

86
00:07:35,380 --> 00:07:36,060
Yes, sir!

87
00:07:37,440 --> 00:07:41,120
Hey, Asahi.

88
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:41,700
Huh?

89
00:07:42,900 --> 00:07:44,840
Come on, give us a nice serve!

90
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:47,560
I'm so in the zone right now.

91
00:07:48,860 --> 00:07:50,380
I'll get us one right here!

92
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:55,440
That's out!

93
00:07:57,580 --> 00:07:58,900
Ah, damn it!

94
00:07:59,660 --> 00:08:00,580
Thanks, dude!

95
00:08:06,500 --> 00:08:06,980
Rail!

96
00:08:07,440 --> 00:08:09,140
Nice receive!

97
00:08:11,580 --> 00:08:15,140
From what I've observed, Ushiwaka has only a handful of patterns.

98
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:17,340
He spikes down, he spikes through.

99
00:08:17,620 --> 00:08:19,500
And when we're lucky, we'll get a one-touch.

100
00:08:19,860 --> 00:08:20,600
Or...

101
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:26,920
So if Ushiwaka tries to come in for one of his quick attacks from the right side, he will most likely attempt a cross-court spike.

102
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:28,740
We can shut him out together.

103
00:08:29,820 --> 00:08:31,300
With a two-man block!

104
00:08:33,100 --> 00:08:36,380
We won't have the same advantages as a three-man block, obviously.

105
00:08:36,380 --> 00:08:43,400
But while we are distracting him, it'll give our team's guardian a clear vision of follow-up.

106
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:54,220
There's only one person on the court who's Ushiwaka's equal.

107
00:08:55,100 --> 00:08:55,460
Me.

108
00:08:55,460 --> 00:09:00,080
I absolutely will not let him win!

109
00:09:00,920 --> 00:09:01,620
Nice receive!

110
00:09:01,620 --> 00:09:11,540
Hey, dumbass!

111
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:13,860
Do I need to call Child Protective Services?

112
00:09:14,120 --> 00:09:16,060
You're standing around like a lost kid at the mall!

113
00:09:16,060 --> 00:09:16,580
Sorry!

114
00:09:17,920 --> 00:09:21,000
Coach seems calmer this game, but still has it out for me.

115
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:25,200
Do you know why he always gets the maddest with you, Goshki?

116
00:09:25,540 --> 00:09:26,800
Because I suck, right?

117
00:09:27,060 --> 00:09:29,480
Actually, it's because he expects the most from you.

118
00:09:30,520 --> 00:09:30,760
Huh?

119
00:09:36,620 --> 00:09:38,680
Bring it on!

120
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:41,480
Good grief. What a little lunkhead.

121
00:09:41,880 --> 00:09:43,540
I just told him the honest truth.

122
00:09:46,060 --> 00:09:51,740
You're so slow, Blondie.

123
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:54,400
Blocking is all about reading and intuition.

124
00:09:56,080 --> 00:09:57,760
No, blocking is a system.

125
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:04,520
Hinata!

126
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:08,040
Goshki!

127
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:11,680
Bet this bastard tries to go for a super shark straight again.

128
00:10:12,500 --> 00:10:13,060
Nice!

129
00:10:13,340 --> 00:10:14,840
Hinata's quick with the follow-up!

130
00:10:16,060 --> 00:10:19,760
How did he find an opening?

131
00:10:20,380 --> 00:10:20,600
Huh?

132
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:21,420
What?

133
00:10:21,800 --> 00:10:23,440
He squeezed the ball through there?

134
00:10:23,640 --> 00:10:25,440
That was a fluke shot, huh?

135
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:26,320
Fluke?

136
00:10:26,980 --> 00:10:28,040
Don't be absurd.

137
00:10:28,760 --> 00:10:30,880
Don't you know you can expect these miracle plays?

138
00:10:31,420 --> 00:10:32,780
From aces like me?

139
00:10:32,820 --> 00:10:33,680
Oh, don't even.

140
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:34,840
You're not fooling anybody.

141
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:42,160
So, as amazing as that last play was, we'll just have to kick things up and take the points back in the even more badass way.

142
00:10:42,660 --> 00:10:43,080
Yeah!

143
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:46,200
Nice to see it!

144
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,100
Come on!

145
00:10:52,100 --> 00:10:54,400
Use our numbers to our advantage!

146
00:10:55,080 --> 00:10:56,660
Go for the synchronized attack!

147
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:58,040
Great.

148
00:10:58,200 --> 00:10:59,880
Here comes that damn attack again.

149
00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:01,720
But wait.

150
00:11:01,720 --> 00:11:17,240
They stopped the synchronized attack?

151
00:11:17,240 --> 00:11:18,880
How did that happen?

152
00:11:18,880 --> 00:11:20,460
No.

153
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:24,640
Go for the synchronized attack!

154
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:26,120
The Funnee Team!

155
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:27,060
Go for the ray警!

156
00:11:27,200 --> 00:11:28,200
No.

157
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:28,880
Go for the synchronized attack!

158
00:11:29,520 --> 00:11:31,020
Go for theansing!

159
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:31,520
You won't need my incredible energy in the hasilvy!

160
00:11:31,900 --> 00:11:32,260
Go for the fruit!

161
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:33,740
Go for the national!

162
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:34,880
Go for the finale!

163
00:11:35,260 --> 00:11:36,240
Go for the night!

164
00:11:36,600 --> 00:11:37,100
Go for theки!

165
00:11:37,160 --> 00:11:38,080
Go for the winks!

166
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:38,740
Bang deber!

167
00:11:38,740 --> 00:11:38,840
Go for theкими!

168
00:11:38,980 --> 00:11:39,520
Twitter!

169
00:11:39,520 --> 00:11:39,880
Cl contingent!

170
00:11:40,880 --> 00:11:41,620
Clости!

171
00:11:41,620 --> 00:11:45,960
Their number 12 is sharp.

172
00:11:46,480 --> 00:11:50,660
I think he was able to determine that the entire right side was out of the picture on that play.

173
00:11:50,940 --> 00:11:53,820
And he figured it out by looking at Daichi's position alone.

174
00:11:54,920 --> 00:11:58,180
It's not that a follow-up by Daichi would be impossible or anything,

175
00:11:58,480 --> 00:12:01,080
but I'd say it would be more that the odds were improbable.

176
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:05,380
If only you guys took the game this seriously a few years back.

177
00:12:05,380 --> 00:12:11,620
Oh, hello, sir!

178
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:13,440
At ease, fellas.

179
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:18,160
Although I do clearly remember, you two always going for the ball without thinking.

180
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:21,560
We were doing the best we could, sir.

181
00:12:22,220 --> 00:12:24,240
That Dusty Fossil is the old coach.

182
00:12:24,640 --> 00:12:25,760
He's Yuka's grandpa.

183
00:12:28,760 --> 00:12:29,820
There we go.

184
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:34,560
I see Washijo's still kicking and has assembled yet another solid lineup.

185
00:12:34,560 --> 00:12:36,120
They're a mess.

186
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:39,560
If Karasano hadn't tried to attack all at once,

187
00:12:40,080 --> 00:12:42,780
they might have had some people left to follow up that block.

188
00:12:43,340 --> 00:12:44,420
I have to agree.

189
00:12:45,140 --> 00:12:47,300
Our play styles are completely different.

190
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:51,220
But we both like to steal points by force.

191
00:12:52,020 --> 00:12:54,020
I guess we aren't so different after all.

192
00:12:59,140 --> 00:12:59,660
Yes!

193
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:03,040
This is turning into a battle of philosophies.

194
00:13:04,560 --> 00:13:07,040
It's just like the old days going against Yukai.

195
00:13:07,860 --> 00:13:11,580
These two groups of high schoolers are a good way to settle our score.

196
00:13:12,300 --> 00:13:14,660
It'll determine which of our methods is the strongest.

197
00:13:14,660 --> 00:13:16,100
Lay down a nice one, Daishi!

198
00:13:16,100 --> 00:13:21,700
If Ushiwaka's not serving or receiving,

199
00:13:21,940 --> 00:13:24,120
we should keep everything confined to the left side.

200
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:25,520
We got it!

201
00:13:26,780 --> 00:13:28,100
Nice receive, Rayon!

202
00:13:28,260 --> 00:13:29,400
We force the action.

203
00:13:30,460 --> 00:13:31,980
Force Ushiwaka to attack.

204
00:13:32,020 --> 00:13:32,640
Okay, now!

205
00:13:32,640 --> 00:13:39,700
I've seen Tsukishima irritated plenty of times,

206
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:42,160
but this might be the first time I've seen him this frustrated.

207
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:44,940
Yeah!

208
00:13:44,940 --> 00:13:54,180
Good! It's offline!

209
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:56,960
On my mark!

210
00:13:57,720 --> 00:13:58,760
And now!

211
00:13:58,760 --> 00:14:10,680
If Ushiwaka gets a perfect set and blasts it through our defense,

212
00:14:10,860 --> 00:14:11,920
there's not much we can do.

213
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:15,340
So we'll need to try and stop sets from getting to him.

214
00:14:16,060 --> 00:14:17,880
We'll have center defense step back here

215
00:14:17,880 --> 00:14:20,320
so we can have two or more blockers on him at all times.

216
00:14:20,420 --> 00:14:21,220
The more the better.

217
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:22,380
Stay on his ass!

218
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:25,700
Oh, so just like Inoshita did in our match against Wakuno.

219
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:26,720
Exactly.

220
00:14:27,340 --> 00:14:29,840
And since Tsukishima is doing an exceptional job

221
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:31,540
holding his own as our center blocker,

222
00:14:31,700 --> 00:14:32,820
it's worth trying this.

223
00:14:33,900 --> 00:14:35,440
Only one step back.

224
00:14:37,560 --> 00:14:39,180
But it's an important one.

225
00:14:42,540 --> 00:14:45,680
Even though Tanaka and Hinata have quick reaction times,

226
00:14:45,900 --> 00:14:49,420
we can't let the responsibility of picking up these shots fall on them.

227
00:14:49,780 --> 00:14:50,940
Daishi! Got it!

228
00:14:51,980 --> 00:14:53,460
Tanaka, get the last hit!

229
00:14:53,900 --> 00:14:54,740
Cover the back!

230
00:14:55,700 --> 00:14:57,280
I know where you're going.

231
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:02,220
What the hell?

232
00:15:03,120 --> 00:15:04,400
He stopped it!

233
00:15:07,820 --> 00:15:09,960
It's your miracle boy!

234
00:15:10,820 --> 00:15:11,320
Stop!

235
00:15:11,500 --> 00:15:12,080
Don't!

236
00:15:12,340 --> 00:15:14,000
Pretend-o!

237
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:17,900
Damn it!

238
00:15:17,940 --> 00:15:19,900
Was he seriously able to guess that spike

239
00:15:19,900 --> 00:15:21,860
without knowing exactly where it was coming from?

240
00:15:22,040 --> 00:15:22,500
Nice.

241
00:15:22,860 --> 00:15:23,940
Good job stopping that.

242
00:15:23,940 --> 00:15:24,640
Mm-hmm.

243
00:15:25,060 --> 00:15:25,320
Ha!

244
00:15:25,560 --> 00:15:28,140
I caught him not paying attention to the blockers from his stance.

245
00:15:28,860 --> 00:15:31,100
Besides, spikers are predictable creatures.

246
00:15:31,440 --> 00:15:33,780
They always glance at the direction they're about to shoot.

247
00:15:33,780 --> 00:15:39,780
So that's how he decides which way to go.

248
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:45,100
I guess Karasuno's number five's body language said he was planning on hitting it there all along.

249
00:15:45,580 --> 00:15:47,040
Nintendo picked up on him.

250
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:47,540
Relax.

251
00:15:47,900 --> 00:15:48,480
It's fine.

252
00:15:48,480 --> 00:15:50,640
That was a pretty amazing block we just witnessed.

253
00:15:50,640 --> 00:15:52,220
Shut your face!

254
00:15:52,440 --> 00:15:53,480
Not too shabby.

255
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:58,440
They're pulling off these high-level moves without trying to outthink themselves.

256
00:15:59,520 --> 00:16:02,240
But their opponents are called champions for a reason.

257
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:05,360
They'll need to pull out all the stops if they are going to win.

258
00:16:05,360 --> 00:16:07,320
Give us a nice serve, Ushiwaka!

259
00:16:18,700 --> 00:16:19,260
Sorry!

260
00:16:20,820 --> 00:16:22,440
What the heck just happened?

261
00:16:22,700 --> 00:16:25,440
How in the hell is that Ushiwaka guy even a real person?

262
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:27,360
Do it again!

263
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:33,900
Cover that!

264
00:16:34,580 --> 00:16:37,380
I'm not going to allow them to extend this lead anymore!

265
00:16:38,460 --> 00:16:38,980
Wait.

266
00:16:39,220 --> 00:16:40,140
That's a low block.

267
00:16:42,880 --> 00:16:43,400
Yeah!

268
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:46,580
All yours, man!

269
00:16:48,260 --> 00:16:48,780
Hey.

270
00:16:49,740 --> 00:16:52,500
How about you start scoring some points while you're up in front?

271
00:16:52,980 --> 00:16:54,220
We could kind of use...

272
00:16:54,220 --> 00:16:56,520
I know!

273
00:16:57,360 --> 00:16:59,260
Oh, hey.

274
00:16:59,400 --> 00:17:00,180
Come to think of it.

275
00:17:00,620 --> 00:17:03,540
Didn't Ushiwaka have some words with Hinata in between the sets?

276
00:17:03,840 --> 00:17:04,120
Oh.

277
00:17:04,640 --> 00:17:04,940
Yeah.

278
00:17:05,320 --> 00:17:08,380
Shrimps are only for eating, not for playing volleyball.

279
00:17:08,880 --> 00:17:09,760
That's what he said.

280
00:17:10,380 --> 00:17:10,860
Seriously?

281
00:17:11,560 --> 00:17:13,140
That wasn't just as complex?

282
00:17:13,780 --> 00:17:15,620
That's exactly what I thought also.

283
00:17:15,980 --> 00:17:17,920
But that seems to be exactly what he meant.

284
00:17:18,580 --> 00:17:20,940
Hinata's probably stewing on the inside right now.

285
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:23,120
You're not really one to talk.

286
00:17:23,800 --> 00:17:24,800
If you think about it.

287
00:17:24,800 --> 00:17:29,920
Hinata wouldn't be here if he was the type to get his spirit broken over a few insults.

288
00:17:35,560 --> 00:17:36,500
That's the cap.

289
00:17:36,800 --> 00:17:37,060
Good.

290
00:17:37,280 --> 00:17:37,540
Good.

291
00:17:39,060 --> 00:17:40,040
Sorry about that.

292
00:17:40,260 --> 00:17:40,720
It's short.

293
00:17:42,700 --> 00:17:43,260
Rayon!

294
00:17:43,260 --> 00:17:48,700
Since I outclassed you in pure height, you think your clumsy technique will make up for it?

295
00:17:50,540 --> 00:17:51,220
Damn it.

296
00:17:51,780 --> 00:17:54,040
Tall guys don't know how easy they've got it.

297
00:17:54,220 --> 00:17:55,260
It makes me jealous, but...

298
00:17:55,260 --> 00:18:00,380
He's getting ready to block, but he's running in like...

299
00:18:00,380 --> 00:18:02,200
He's about to spike.

300
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:04,260
That approaching run...

301
00:18:05,100 --> 00:18:07,460
Makes him look like he has weanies.

302
00:18:07,460 --> 00:18:18,580
He stopped it!

303
00:18:20,220 --> 00:18:21,460
I might envy your height...

304
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:25,080
But I can use mine to my advantage as well.

305
00:18:25,880 --> 00:18:26,940
How do you like that?

306
00:18:28,580 --> 00:18:29,800
Karasuno got a break.

307
00:18:30,220 --> 00:18:31,420
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

308
00:18:31,420 --> 00:18:35,960
Did my vision just fail me, or did that little number 10 fella finally get a decent block?

309
00:18:36,280 --> 00:18:37,140
Well, I don't know.

310
00:18:37,320 --> 00:18:40,600
Number 10 plays kind of erratic, so I think it was probably a fluke.

311
00:18:42,920 --> 00:18:46,480
Maybe you should go sit up there with Mr. Grumpy Pants, Mr. Early Critical.

312
00:18:46,880 --> 00:18:47,280
True.

313
00:18:47,840 --> 00:18:50,560
But if it's not a fluke, this game's about to change.

314
00:18:50,760 --> 00:18:51,420
Big time.

315
00:18:54,060 --> 00:18:54,420
Nishinoya.

316
00:18:56,420 --> 00:18:57,640
Hinata to the rescue!

317
00:18:57,980 --> 00:18:59,900
He should just do that every time!

318
00:18:59,900 --> 00:19:01,060
No, no, no!

319
00:19:01,520 --> 00:19:05,380
He can't do the same thing every time, and besides that, won't counter fast attacks!

320
00:19:05,860 --> 00:19:08,060
And it would also do a number on his stamina.

321
00:19:08,620 --> 00:19:10,960
Middle blockers jump around the most as it is.

322
00:19:11,280 --> 00:19:12,840
Plus, Hinata is working overtime.

323
00:19:13,200 --> 00:19:15,180
Jumping at full power to compensate for his height.

324
00:19:15,540 --> 00:19:19,660
Funny that's coming from you, a guy who would invent new ways to slack off during a game.

325
00:19:19,920 --> 00:19:20,780
Oh, you know it!

326
00:19:23,260 --> 00:19:26,180
Can't complain if you were actually good while playing lazy.

327
00:19:27,580 --> 00:19:28,620
Get it, Rayon!

328
00:19:28,620 --> 00:19:30,440
One more time!

329
00:19:32,440 --> 00:19:35,460
I knew that was gonna happen.

330
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:37,200
My God, I'm sorry!

331
00:19:38,020 --> 00:19:38,600
It's okay.

332
00:19:38,880 --> 00:19:41,320
Think about where you're going, you tiny dumbass!

333
00:19:41,740 --> 00:19:43,800
Hinata, I've got a message from Coach.

334
00:19:44,180 --> 00:19:46,600
Forget what you know about jumping, let's try something new.

335
00:19:46,860 --> 00:19:49,400
Instead of jumping up, try doing a sideways sweep.

336
00:19:49,760 --> 00:19:50,620
So you guys can...

337
00:19:50,620 --> 00:19:52,580
Support his jump from the sides!

338
00:19:52,580 --> 00:19:53,500
Got it!

339
00:19:57,660 --> 00:19:59,200
My timing's still off!

340
00:19:59,380 --> 00:20:00,500
I hope I can nail this!

341
00:20:01,840 --> 00:20:02,900
Hit it right back!

342
00:20:03,040 --> 00:20:03,460
Kill it!

343
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:07,740
If you could play a good game of volleyball while being lazy,

344
00:20:08,400 --> 00:20:09,080
cat gripe,

345
00:20:09,080 --> 00:20:12,040
but a small fry over there

346
00:20:12,040 --> 00:20:15,180
has no choice but to jump.

347
00:20:20,180 --> 00:20:21,320
Nice kill, Hinata!

348
00:20:21,320 --> 00:20:26,440
I didn't expect to see you.

349
00:20:26,780 --> 00:20:28,280
I thought you said you weren't coming

350
00:20:28,280 --> 00:20:30,880
since this game's outcome would piss you off no matter who won.

351
00:20:31,740 --> 00:20:33,200
I might have said something like that,

352
00:20:33,240 --> 00:20:34,700
but I didn't come here to watch someone win.

353
00:20:34,740 --> 00:20:36,100
I came to watch someone lose.

354
00:20:36,220 --> 00:20:37,120
Such a piece of crap.

355
00:20:37,120 --> 00:20:39,960
I can't wallow in self-pity all day.

356
00:20:40,780 --> 00:20:42,580
So I see Karasuno's number 10

357
00:20:42,580 --> 00:20:44,540
is doing laps around the court as usual.

358
00:20:45,040 --> 00:20:47,420
The little guy is definitely a monster.

359
00:20:48,380 --> 00:20:50,680
I must say I feel sorry for anyone

360
00:20:50,680 --> 00:20:52,080
who has to play with him.

361
00:20:57,500 --> 00:20:58,340
It's me!

362
00:20:58,800 --> 00:20:59,320
Tanaka!

363
00:20:59,540 --> 00:20:59,860
Yeah!

364
00:21:05,500 --> 00:21:06,860
Let him have it, Suki!

365
00:21:06,860 --> 00:21:11,920
The jump's peak!

366
00:21:12,160 --> 00:21:12,780
The jump's peak!

367
00:21:12,880 --> 00:21:13,540
The jump's peak!

368
00:21:13,920 --> 00:21:14,700
The jump's...

369
00:21:14,700 --> 00:21:15,700
peak!

370
00:21:18,080 --> 00:21:18,520
Front!

371
00:21:18,720 --> 00:21:19,000
Front!

372
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:20,840
Left side!

373
00:21:23,420 --> 00:21:24,400
One touch!

374
00:21:24,720 --> 00:21:25,560
Chance ball!

375
00:21:27,420 --> 00:21:27,980
Pushybaka!

376
00:21:29,340 --> 00:21:30,400
Come on, Hinata!

377
00:21:31,560 --> 00:21:32,420
I'll be here.

378
00:21:33,480 --> 00:21:33,960
Support!

379
00:21:36,860 --> 00:21:39,880
It's a one touch!

380
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:41,740
I got it!

381
00:21:43,420 --> 00:21:44,820
Don't fade on me, Hinata!

382
00:21:45,140 --> 00:21:46,500
Why don't you shut up?

383
00:21:47,780 --> 00:21:50,060
He's really running all the way to the other side?

384
00:21:50,700 --> 00:21:51,160
Oh, crap.

385
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:51,840
I got it!

386
00:21:51,840 --> 00:21:52,080
I got it!

387
00:21:52,080 --> 00:21:52,120
I got it!

388
00:21:52,120 --> 00:21:52,340
I got it!

389
00:21:57,780 --> 00:21:58,640
Yeah!

390
00:22:00,700 --> 00:22:02,020
Break support, Tanaka!

391
00:22:02,160 --> 00:22:02,800
Well done!

392
00:22:03,040 --> 00:22:06,200
An upperclassman, his only job is to help those younger than he!

393
00:22:06,560 --> 00:22:07,340
Nice haiku!

394
00:22:08,340 --> 00:22:09,300
It's a freak!

395
00:22:10,300 --> 00:22:10,820
Hinata!

396
00:22:10,820 --> 00:22:12,260
Nice one touch!

397
00:22:12,740 --> 00:22:14,040
Karasuna's really reckless.

398
00:22:14,500 --> 00:22:16,920
First that sloppy, synchronized attack, and now this?

399
00:22:18,220 --> 00:22:20,200
Let them wear themselves down.

400
00:22:20,660 --> 00:22:22,960
They might have these tricky techniques and combinations,

401
00:22:23,320 --> 00:22:26,540
but our sheer power will win in the end.

402
00:22:27,280 --> 00:22:29,580
If a player's height and physical ability

403
00:22:29,580 --> 00:22:31,820
were the only determining factor to win a game,

404
00:22:32,320 --> 00:22:35,200
then this match would have been settled a long time ago.

405
00:22:36,100 --> 00:22:39,320
But because there's so much more to the game,

406
00:22:39,320 --> 00:22:42,020
it makes this match-up all the more interesting.

407
00:23:09,320 --> 00:23:11,320
Thank you.

408
00:23:39,320 --> 00:23:41,320
Thank you.

409
00:24:09,320 --> 00:24:17,100
You're clicking your tongue more than usual, Tsukishima.

410
00:24:17,320 --> 00:24:18,260
You sound like a clock.

411
00:24:18,520 --> 00:24:19,060
A clock?

412
00:24:19,240 --> 00:24:21,060
What the hell does a clock have to do with volleyball?

413
00:24:21,400 --> 00:24:23,040
Just focus on the match, you two.

414
00:24:23,940 --> 00:24:26,280
Next Haikyuu, the chemical changes of meeting.

